config BR2_PACKAGE_HAOS_COMPUTE_NVIDIA
	bool "NVIDIA proprietary compute stack (open kernel modules + UVM + driver libs)"
	default y if BR2_PACKAGE_HAOS_GPU_AI_ALL
	depends on BR2_x86_64
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	select BR2_PACKAGE_HAOS_NVIDIA_CONTAINER_TOOLKIT
	help
	  Builds the NVIDIA "open" GPU kernel modules against the HAOS kernel and
	  installs the matching proprietary user-space driver libraries required
	  on the HOST:

	    Kernel modules : nvidia.ko, nvidia-uvm.ko, nvidia-modeset.ko,
	                     nvidia-drm.ko, nvidia-peermem.ko
	    Host libraries : libcuda, libnvidia-ml, libnvidia-ptxjitcompiler
	    Helpers        : nvidia-modprobe (setuid, creates /dev nodes), nvidia-smi

	  The OPEN modules are used because they are the vendor-recommended and
	  build-reliable path for Turing (RTX 20xx) and newer GPUs on recent
	  kernels. This stack therefore requires a GPU of Turing generation or
	  later.

	  IMPORTANT: the CUDA *runtime* (libcudart, libnvrtc, cuBLAS, ...) is NOT
	  installed on the host. It ships inside the add-on container. The NVIDIA
	  Container Toolkit (auto-selected) injects the host driver libraries above
	  into the container at run time, which is why only the driver-provided
	  libraries live in the base OS.

if BR2_PACKAGE_HAOS_COMPUTE_NVIDIA

config BR2_PACKAGE_HAOS_COMPUTE_NVIDIA_VERSION
	string "NVIDIA driver version"
	default "595.84"
	help
	  Driver/branch version. Must be a release whose open kernel modules
	  support the pinned HAOS kernel. Bump this together with any kernel jump;
	  the CI kernel<->driver gate fails the build on an incompatible pair.

	  Kernel reference points (verify against NVIDIA's Unix driver page):
	    535 -> up to ~6.5    550 -> up to ~6.11
	    580.126.18 fixes the kernel 6.19 module build
	    595.84 = current Production Branch (covers 6.12 through 6.18/6.19-era kernels)
	  The repo now targets HAOS 18.3 (kernel 6.18.52); 595.84 covers the 6.18 line,
	  so no driver change is needed for the bump. The last line fully hardware-
	  proven was 17.3 (kernel 6.12.85, where 595.84 built and ran on the RTX 4090);
	  the 18.3 open-module build against 6.18.52 is NOT yet device-verified - the CI
	  preflight gate checks the kernel<->driver pairing and asset reachability, and
	  the actual open-module compile is proven only by a green build + flash.

endif
